    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδευκής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
		</span></i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέθρψ ἀδευκέϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.489
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδευκέα πότμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.245
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῆμιν ἀδευκέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.273
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.267
			</span></i>, etc. (Expl. by Scholl. either (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦκος</span>, q.v.) <i>not sweet,</i> i. e. <i>bitter,
				cruel</i>, or (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεύκει</span>)
				<i>unexpected</i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.φωνή</span> expl. as
				<i>not imitative</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυδευκής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				5.38
			</span></i>.)</div>
